  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Unless there is compelling reason not to, Fedora should follow the Maven standard directory layout as described here: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://maven.apache.org/guides/introduction/introduction-to-the-standard-directory-layout.html"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://maven.apache.org/guides/introduction/introduction-to-the-standard-directory-layout.html",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Examples of where Fedora seems to arbitrarily diverge: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1) assemblies in src/main/resources/assemblies rather than src/main/assemblies",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) config files almost everywhere except src/main/config",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) LICENSE.txt",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "4) use of src/main/resources as a general dumping ground (e.g. shell scripts), rather than for resources (e.g. properties files) intended to be made available on the classpath",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
